00:20:31.600 --> 00:20:36.300
To the gospel even much more
than what we could ever imagine.

00:20:36.460 --> 00:20:41.718
And so we witnessed tribes coming
to Jesus that has never heard

00:20:41.718 --> 00:20:47.060
the gospel, that is all over these
areas that we would fly into.

00:20:47.060 --> 00:20:51.288
You. And when Carl, when we
would fly into these areas,

00:20:51.288 --> 00:20:55.900
it was for sure, they had never
heard the name Jesus before.

00:20:55.940 --> 00:20:59.720
And through the Holy Spirit,
we began to teach and train.

00:20:59.740 --> 00:21:03.333
Train and train evangelists
to where now it's very few

00:21:03.333 --> 00:21:06.660
remaining that those tribes
are unreached anymore.

00:21:06.700 --> 00:21:08.560
Is there work to be done?

00:21:08.600 --> 00:21:12.830
Absolutely. But there's a
church established that can

00:21:12.830 --> 00:21:16.900
continue to spread the
gospel throughout the tribe.

00:21:17.240 --> 00:21:19.580
And so that was the beginning.

00:21:19.620 --> 00:21:23.617
All that sounds very glorious
but I'm telling you that day

00:21:23.617 --> 00:21:27.890
by day it wasn't always the
easiest life but the Lord has been

00:21:27.890 --> 00:21:31.680
so gracious and I would not
change my life or anything.

00:21:32.020 --> 00:21:35.824
Throughout that on my side
I was not always able to

00:21:35.824 --> 00:21:38.659
go in the helicopter because you know,

00:21:38.659 --> 00:21:43.060
there's a few there's few seats
and being a wife and a mom.

00:21:43.100 --> 00:21:47.460
And, you know, a lot of my
work was around where I lived.

00:21:47.500 --> 00:21:51.472
And so I began to look
at social, you know,

00:21:51.472 --> 00:21:56.460
more of the poverty and the
social issues in Ethiopia.

00:21:56.500 --> 00:21:59.793
So, and as we were reaching unreached,

00:21:59.793 --> 00:22:05.860
and that became our priority,
there's you can't close your eyes to the

00:22:10.440 --> 00:22:13.129
I don't think it's
either or that's another

00:22:13.129 --> 00:22:15.880
language you're going
to hear from me a lot.

00:22:15.920 --> 00:22:20.212
There's no either or there's not an
either or in the sense of you know

00:22:20.212 --> 00:22:24.320
what I mean in the sense of I'm
going to reach unreached and that's

00:22:24.320 --> 00:22:28.060
much more important than my
neighbor here and no, it's a both

00:22:28.060 --> 00:22:31.520
And the Lord desires
everyone to be reached.

00:22:31.520 --> 00:22:36.100
It is much more difficult
to reach some than others.

00:22:36.140 --> 00:22:42.359
So we want to put our hands and our
feet and give our lives to who has

00:22:42.359 --> 00:22:48.400
never heard, but it's not a more
important to read them the reaching

00:22:48.400 --> 00:22:51.960
Here. But all to say that.

00:22:52.000 --> 00:22:56.415
We were there for 17 years
and I began to go into

00:22:56.415 --> 00:23:00.740
social a lot of social
work worked with HIV AIDS

00:23:01.000 --> 00:23:03.660
Worked a lot with women and children

00:23:04.020 --> 00:23:06.220
Started projects to help women.

00:23:06.260 --> 00:23:08.720
There's a lot of human trafficking.

00:23:08.940 --> 00:23:11.478
At that time, we didn't
call it human trafficking,

00:23:11.478 --> 00:23:13.000
but that's exactly what it is.

00:23:13.040 --> 00:23:16.320
And I'm telling you,
the women that we reach

00:23:16.600 --> 00:23:20.392
It would cost like 50 cents
for a man to sleep with them

00:23:20.392 --> 00:23:24.185
and they're in these little
huts and it's just a curtain

00:23:24.185 --> 00:23:27.300
with terrible, dirty,
like makeshift mattress.

00:23:27.300 --> 00:23:28.920
And that's what it looked like.

00:23:28.960 --> 00:23:32.780
So we rescued many women out of that,

00:23:32.780 --> 00:23:37.840
helped many children that
their moms died of HIV.

00:23:37.880 --> 00:23:40.410
I can't even tell you how
many women I have done

00:23:40.410 --> 00:23:42.940
their funeral and we have
helped their children.

00:23:43.000 --> 00:23:48.031
So as we were reaching unreached,
I was very involved with the social

00:23:48.031 --> 00:23:52.260
work of Ethiopia and it's still
near and dear to my heart.

00:23:52.300 --> 00:23:55.279
Actually, my daughter, Abigail, Gabby,

00:23:55.279 --> 00:23:59.747
mentioned her and I don't know
if you heard her story but

00:23:59.747 --> 00:24:04.920
she was one of the kids we just
the Lord brought her to us and she

00:24:04.920 --> 00:24:09.118
Was HIV positive she was dying
only she was several months

00:24:09.118 --> 00:24:13.171
old only weighed four pounds
and the Lord just we prayed

00:24:13.171 --> 00:24:17.080
for her and Carl prayed and
said Lord if you will heal

00:24:17.080 --> 00:24:23.339
This baby we would love to adopt her
and the Lord healed and she was positive

00:24:23.339 --> 00:24:29.680
and test after test after test after test,
she, she tested negative of HIV, so

00:24:29.680 --> 00:24:32.260
She's a miracle..

00:24:32.360 --> 00:24:37.740
That's just one of the miracles and it
all we raised four children in Ethiopia.

00:24:37.740 --> 00:24:43.700
But and so we came to a place and
we even worked with Mass Evangelism.

00:24:43.740 --> 00:24:46.762
So Carl and I, we lived
there for almost 20 years,

00:24:46.762 --> 00:24:48.877
it's like you got to do everything,

00:24:48.877 --> 00:24:51.597
you know, and we worked
with Mass Evangelism,

00:24:51.597 --> 00:24:54.800
we had projects, we had a
helicopter base, we worked.

00:24:55.020 --> 00:24:57.374
And there was times where
we had several missionaries

00:24:57.374 --> 00:24:59.640
working with us and the
Lord is doing great things.

00:24:59.680 --> 00:25:03.289
And you know what, the mission
field became easy for me,

00:25:03.289 --> 00:25:06.962
it became home to me, home my
children and that's what it

00:25:06.962 --> 00:25:10.700
became very easy and I can
remember like it was yesterday.

00:25:10.740 --> 00:25:16.830
The Lord woke me up and the Lord wrote
Carl up and we did not know you know I

00:25:16.830 --> 00:25:23.000
just got up and I was sitting in our
living room in Ethiopia and the Lord woke

00:25:23.000 --> 00:25:27.249
Up Carl and exactly at the same
time it came out of our mouth

00:25:27.249 --> 00:25:31.220
we're to start a school we're
to start a training school.

00:25:31.860 --> 00:25:33.940
And what did that look like?

00:25:33.980 --> 00:25:39.620
And anyway, we began to
investigate, seek and search how

00:25:39.620 --> 00:25:45.260
the Lord wants us and we
decided we would take one year.

00:25:45.300 --> 00:25:46.640
And we gave

00:25:46.900 --> 00:25:51.540
We really trained up our team,
we gave, we handed everything over.

00:25:51.580 --> 00:25:56.400
And let me tell you that everything is
still happening still in Ethiopia today.

00:25:56.440 --> 00:25:59.720
It's like, people are
still doing the work.

00:25:59.720 --> 00:26:01.507
And so after 20 years of,
and it was just like the mission

00:26:01.507 --> 00:26:02.740
work had, like I said, it's became easy.

00:26:02.740 --> 00:26:04.528
We saw hundreds, I can literally
say hundreds of thousands

00:26:04.528 --> 00:26:06.439
of thousands of years of work.
And so we've had a lot of work.

00:26:06.439 --> 00:26:08.318
There's still, I mean, we've
had a little bit of muddy waters

00:26:08.318 --> 00:26:09.890
recently, because that's
another story, my parents,

00:26:09.890 --> 00:26:12.140
they started a farm there, a flower
farm, and then my dad suddenly passed

00:26:12.140 --> 00:26:15.440
Away So we're walking through
some muddy waters with that.

00:26:15.480 --> 00:26:18.500
But I can say all the
work is still continuing.

00:26:19.560 --> 00:26:22.961
And so after 20 years of,
and it was just like,

00:26:22.961 --> 00:26:26.580
the mission work had,
like I said, it became easy.

00:26:26.620 --> 00:26:29.749
We saw hundreds, I can literally
say hundreds of thousands

00:26:29.749 --> 00:26:32.500
of people saved during the
time that we were there.

00:26:32.520 --> 00:26:36.060
We saw so many people
delivered, healed, set free.

00:26:36.100 --> 00:26:39.660
We became family with
several people there.

00:26:39.660 --> 00:26:46.230
And to come back to America to
start a school was as difficult

00:26:46.230 --> 00:26:51.740
as going to Ethiopia with
the agreement that I would

00:26:51.740 --> 00:26:53.100
Not ever

00:27:04.840 --> 00:27:17.320
I would not even leave the country for

00:27:17.320 --> 00:27:18.520
Four years.

00:27:19.260 --> 00:27:22.480
That difficult to go back.

00:27:22.480 --> 00:27:28.380
And that this has to be much more than
just Carl and I answering the call.

00:27:28.420 --> 00:27:34.833
There needs to be some deposit and
discipling of others in order for

00:27:34.833 --> 00:27:40.680
them to answer because it's going
to take the church to engage

00:27:40.680 --> 00:27:43.120
In unreached people groups.

00:27:43.160 --> 00:27:44.900
And I'm talking about the whole church.

00:27:44.940 --> 00:27:48.150
If it's in America or if it's overseas,

00:27:48.150 --> 00:27:54.240
we have to lean into, lean into the
call and to take other people with us.

00:27:54.280 --> 00:27:57.200
So Carl, Carl and I, we came to
this place. It was very difficult.

00:27:57.240 --> 00:28:00.140
It was very difficult.
Am I boring you with all this?

00:28:01.420 --> 00:28:05.300
It's good just for you to
connect with the DNA, right?

00:28:05.340 --> 00:28:09.980
Yes. So we came by faith.

00:28:09.980 --> 00:28:14.180
We didn't have a home. I had four
children, my two oldest ones.

00:28:14.180 --> 00:28:17.020
Now they're they both live in Sweden.

00:28:17.060 --> 00:28:21.223
My oldest daughter they were
very upset, sad to leave Ethiopia

00:28:21.223 --> 00:28:25.387
because that was home for them
and coming back just one little

00:28:25.387 --> 00:28:29.080
by little the Lord began to
just open doors and send us

00:28:29.080 --> 00:28:33.115
People and the classes some of
them have been big some of them

00:28:33.115 --> 00:28:37.346
have been small but many missionaries
have been trained and going

00:28:37.346 --> 00:28:40.860
back to the field and that's
really our ultimate goal.

00:28:40.900 --> 00:28:44.609
Our ultimate goal is not only
to take a six week mission trip,

00:28:44.609 --> 00:28:47.960
which is quite long in
comparison to most mission trips.

00:28:48.000 --> 00:28:54.100
But it is actually to see full-time
missionaries engage and be raised.

00:28:54.340 --> 00:28:59.568
And not only missionaries raised up,
but to go with the idea and understanding

00:28:59.568 --> 00:29:03.120
and training on how to reach
and reach people groups.

00:29:03.120 --> 00:29:05.540
That's what our focus is.

00:29:05.580 --> 00:29:12.100
And so we started, we thought we would
have like a one campus type school.

00:29:12.140 --> 00:29:14.460
This was really a miracle.

00:29:14.600 --> 00:29:17.340
And so we started at a campground.

00:29:17.380 --> 00:29:22.840
And we did all of this work to
campground and that didn't work out.

00:29:22.880 --> 00:29:26.744
And so we were a little
bit disappointed in that,

00:29:26.744 --> 00:29:31.160
disorientated and wondering
what will be our next steps.

00:29:31.160 --> 00:29:36.660
And the Lord really opened the door
for us to go into a local church.

00:29:36.700 --> 00:29:38.380
And it's like we didn't have that idea.

00:29:38.420 --> 00:29:41.873
It was just because we had this
resist or this type of resistance

00:29:41.873 --> 00:29:45.060
that caused us to make the
decision to go into local church.

00:29:45.100 --> 00:29:49.454
And now we can have Mission 111
in any local church and it's

00:29:49.454 --> 00:29:53.664
really through the church
called and we're sent and that's

00:29:53.664 --> 00:29:57.220
just part of the idea with
mission 111 we are not

00:29:57.220 --> 00:30:01.638
Disconnected from the church or
we're not a sub branch of the church

00:30:01.638 --> 00:30:05.666
we are the church and we are
sent by the church and the church

00:30:05.666 --> 00:30:09.240
is not our enemy in any way
but it is through the local

00:30:09.240 --> 00:30:14.600
Church jesus called the local
church and he said upon this truth.

00:30:14.680 --> 00:30:20.020
I will the gates of hell will not
prevail against whom his church.

00:30:20.060 --> 00:30:26.349
So we are that church and we're meant to
work together to be together to be sent

00:30:26.349 --> 00:30:32.480
to be to be supported by to go with and
to do fulfill it finish the assignment

00:30:32.480 --> 00:30:35.640
Together. It's not meant
to do it independently.

00:30:35.840 --> 00:30:40.349
And so we're here today after 10
years we have schools like actually

00:30:40.349 --> 00:30:44.460
right now I think we have a
mission while I was full that's in

00:30:44.460 --> 00:30:48.240
session and Sri Lanka,
I believe they have about 20 young

00:30:48.240 --> 00:30:54.596
People would be great to even get to
know them a little bit if it's possible,

00:30:54.596 --> 00:31:00.540
through technology to see what they're
doing but I'm finding and reached

00:31:00.540 --> 00:31:06.160
And chronologically storing and
you're going to learn that method.

00:31:06.560 --> 00:31:10.426
Through chronological Bible stories
they're able to witness to people

00:31:10.426 --> 00:31:13.900
who've never heard in groups
that have never heard the gospel.

00:31:13.940 --> 00:31:17.440
And so we have schools going
on and things going on.

00:31:18.080 --> 00:31:21.160
We have a school in
Canada, a few in Sweden

00:31:21.800 --> 00:31:25.468
And different parts of the world.
So I'm happy that we get

00:31:25.468 --> 00:31:29.200
to, but not all of them get to
hear from Carl and his life.

00:31:29.240 --> 00:31:33.000
And right here we, this is your
class, we will teach you live.

00:31:33.000 --> 00:31:38.251
So that's just a little basis
of what Mission 111 is all

00:31:38.251 --> 00:31:43.220
about, how it was formed,
where the vision came from.

00:31:43.260 --> 00:31:47.220
But I know for some, we seem very narrow.

00:31:47.260 --> 00:31:50.680
Our narrowness is this,
we care about our students.

00:31:50.720 --> 00:31:55.137
We care so much about you and
we desire we'll walk with you

00:31:55.137 --> 00:31:59.480
through first getting saved
into sending you to the field.

00:31:59.520 --> 00:32:01.560
And once you're there,
we'll receive you back.

00:32:01.600 --> 00:32:04.289
I mean, we walk with
all of our missionaries,

00:32:04.289 --> 00:32:06.680
but actually our, and that's part of it.

00:32:06.720 --> 00:32:10.067
And it's not, like I said,
it's not an either,

00:32:10.067 --> 00:32:14.361
or it's a both and, but our
priority is for people who have

00:32:14.361 --> 00:32:18.800
never had, they do not have a
chance to hear the gospel and a

00:32:18.800 --> 00:32:20.380
Clear presentation of Jesus.

00:32:20.420 --> 00:32:24.120
And you can think in our nation today,
we have a church on every corner.

00:32:24.120 --> 00:32:30.356
We have Christian messages going around
the world that there are people that

00:32:30.356 --> 00:32:36.100
are, they born, they live and die
without ever hearing the name Jesus.

00:32:36.440 --> 00:32:41.004
And the reason why they have not
heard is because there are boundaries,

00:32:41.004 --> 00:32:44.732
or there is a set of circumstances,
or more than anything,

00:32:44.732 --> 00:32:48.460
people have never gone to them
to tell them about the good

00:32:48.460 --> 00:32:52.160
News of the gospel. That is
our priority of Mission 111.

00:32:52.200 --> 00:32:54.520
That is the heartbeat of Mission 111.

00:32:54.560 --> 00:32:56.300
So are our trips extreme?

00:32:56.300 --> 00:32:58.080
Yeah.

00:32:58.080 --> 00:33:00.420
Is there a little bit of suffering? Yeah.

00:33:00.460 --> 00:33:02.480
But if I can do it, anyone can do it.

00:33:02.520 --> 00:33:05.160
We can do it. And we can do it together.

00:33:05.200 --> 00:33:07.746
And that's what I love.
There's no greater thing

00:33:07.746 --> 00:33:10.080
is to suffer together
with another believer.

00:33:10.120 --> 00:33:13.996
So we will get close, but we
will also get to share and

00:33:13.996 --> 00:33:17.660
seeing people that's never
heard to hear the gospel.

00:33:17.700 --> 00:33:19.440
So that's the heartbeat.

00:33:19.700 --> 00:33:23.240
That's what we. and you'll probably,
you'll hear a Carl's version as well.

00:33:23.280 --> 00:33:27.380
But any questions in that
before I get started?

00:33:28.300 --> 00:33:30.540
In my class and what
my class is all about?

00:33:30.580 --> 00:33:36.531
My class is very personal. It's all
based on kind of my journey of being

00:33:36.531 --> 00:33:42.400
a full-time missionary for 17 years
and some of my reflections of that.

00:33:42.440 --> 00:33:44.840
So my class is very personal

00:33:45.660 --> 00:33:51.240
And it's really discipleship
through missions.

00:33:51.280 --> 00:33:56.467
That's what it's like how I it's
amazing how my life was just

00:33:56.467 --> 00:34:01.740
transformed spiritually in every
way through the mission call.

00:34:01.780 --> 00:34:07.113
So that is kind of the framework of
what we're going to be digging into

00:34:07.113 --> 00:34:11.920
in the word of God and just through
stories that I have for you.

00:34:11.960 --> 00:34:17.620
So we will be looking a little bit
about current issues you know with some

00:34:18.710 --> 00:34:23.393
Of with refugees or with issues of social

00:34:23.393 --> 00:34:28.190
injustices as well, so through this class.

00:34:28.490 --> 00:34:29.690
Any questions?

00:34:30.110 --> 00:34:35.450
So we'll go a little bit
through the class, if you will.

00:34:35.490 --> 00:34:40.430
And then I'm not gonna hold you very
long because it's actually next week.

00:34:40.430 --> 00:34:45.596
That is when I'm really gonna start
teaching, but I just have a few thoughts

00:34:45.596 --> 00:34:50.490
just to put a little bit of, you know,
to make our wheels start turning.

00:34:50.610 --> 00:34:54.537
But you will see in the
syllabus, if you go on Canvas

00:34:54.537 --> 00:34:58.686
and just see my class, I only
allowed you to look at the

00:34:58.686 --> 00:35:02.390
first two weeks and I
wanted you to read the book.

00:35:02.430 --> 00:35:05.167
It's the first time I've
used it, but I like,

00:35:05.167 --> 00:35:08.695
and you can tell me your opinion
since it's the first time

00:35:08.695 --> 00:35:12.770
I had other textbooks, but I wanted
to change that up a little bit.

00:35:12.810 --> 00:35:16.470
I just finished my master's
degree in a leadership program.

00:35:16.510 --> 00:35:20.770
And one of my mentors,
he actually is very missional.

00:35:20.810 --> 00:35:24.348
He used a lot of the thought process of NT

00:35:24.348 --> 00:35:27.550
Wright, if you've heard of theologian.

00:35:27.550 --> 00:35:31.630
And so I'm going to, and I really
like, it resonated with me.

00:35:31.670 --> 00:35:35.890
So your book is by the author NT Wright.

00:35:35.890 --> 00:35:41.470
And I have another one from NT Wright
that is called the mission of God.

00:35:41.790 --> 00:35:45.659
And what I love about his
whole thought process is

00:35:45.659 --> 00:35:49.450
that God from the beginning
was a God of mission.

00:35:49.490 --> 00:35:53.250
It wasn't like, oh, all of
a sudden he's missional.

00:35:53.290 --> 00:35:56.470
God from the very beginning was missional.

00:35:56.470 --> 00:36:01.490
And he and he created us to
participate in his big mission.

00:36:01.530 --> 00:36:04.570
And he did not use
anything except for people.

00:36:04.570 --> 00:36:09.550
His created image bearers
to bring out his mission.

00:36:09.590 --> 00:36:12.770
So that's kind of like
the NT Wright theology.

00:36:12.810 --> 00:36:16.050
That's a theology. It's called Missio Dei.

00:36:16.090 --> 00:36:18.230
And so that's the reason why I chose him.

00:36:18.270 --> 00:36:20.450
You can critique that and
let me know what you think.

00:36:20.490 --> 00:36:22.290
I personally like it a lot.

00:36:22.330 --> 00:36:24.490
I like his thought process.

00:36:24.530 --> 00:36:28.410
And then the other book I want you
to read is the book of Nehemiah.

00:36:28.450 --> 00:36:30.730
I'm going to use a lot of
Nehemiah out of his book.

00:36:30.770 --> 00:36:33.571
I don't know if you've
studied Nehemiah at all,

00:36:33.571 --> 00:36:36.670
But I want to study Nehemiah
in a missional context.

00:36:36.710 --> 00:36:40.100
And I think there's a lot of discipleship

00:36:40.100 --> 00:36:43.490
principles that we can learn through him.

00:36:44.450 --> 00:36:47.970
It's like twofold. He prays.

00:36:48.350 --> 00:36:50.950
He deals with social issues.

00:36:50.990 --> 00:36:53.950
He goes out by faith.
